       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That is twice the labeled maximum for adults, which is 3,200 mg/day under prescription dosing. A dose that high raises the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, and normal kidney and liver function doesn't change that.\n\nHere are some options within the limit:\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), which is the maximum.\n- **600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day).\n- **400 mg PO every 4\u20136 hours as needed**, for pain or fever.\n\nYou may have meant 1600 mg as the total daily dose, for example 400 mg four times daily. Please check that.\n\nTell me which regimen you want and I'll enter it right away. If you need more analgesia than the maximum ibuprofen dose gives, you could add acetaminophen or another agent. I can enter that too."
